  "details": "Udon is cumbersome, needs a lot of technical knowledge to operate, and obtaining prefabs like cyantrigger is difficult and out of the way, especially for people in non-english speaking parts if the world.\nOn top of that, Udon is notoriously slow and malperformant, being a large impactor on many peoples' frames in the game.\nWe need essentially what we had in SDK2, a simplified, albeit limiting, world creation system that uses native unity functions and things that run through internal C# for optimization.\nNeeding to emulate udon simply to make a chill world that has some mirror toggles and a videoplayer is a ridiculous waste of resources.  Especially if the creator wants said world to be very visually detailed.",
